MaterialX is an open standard for representing rich material and
look-development content in computer graphics, enabling its exchange
between applications and renderers.  It is used by OpenUSD, Blender,
Houdini, Maya and many renderers.

This package provides the C++ libraries, the standard data library
(node definitions and implementations), shader generators for GLSL,
MSL (Metal), OSL, MDL and Slang, the GLSL and Metal render modules,
OpenImageIO image loading, and the PyMaterialX Python bindings.
